# n8n

## Mục tiêu

n8n là workflow automation platform cho phép connect apps và automate tasks mà không cần code. Trong Cursor Enterprise Framework, n8n được sử dụng cho business process automation, integration workflows, và data synchronization. Mục tiêu của rule này là hướng dẫn developers trong việc implement và manage n8n workflows một cách hiệu quả và maintainable.

n8n bridges gap giữa no-code tools và custom code, cho phép business users create workflows trong khi developers can extend capabilities when needed.

## Nguyên tắc

**1. Workflow Design**

Clear objectives. Simple flow. Error handling. Idempotent operations.

**2. Node Organization**

Group related nodes. Use sub-nodes for reusability. Clear naming. Proper documentation.

**3. Error Handling**

Try-catch blocks. Retry on failure. Dead letter queues. Alert on errors.

**4. Data Transformation**

Use expressions. Map fields clearly. Validate data. Handle nulls.

**5. Authentication**

Store credentials securely. Rotate tokens. Use OAuth when possible. Avoid hardcoding.

**6. Trigger Design**

Choose appropriate triggers. Webhook for sync. Cron for schedule. Event for async.

**7. Scalability**

Heavy workflows in queue. Batch processing. Avoid long-running workflows. Use pagination.

**8. Version Control**

Export workflows as JSON. Version in Git. Document changes. Use environments.

**9. Monitoring**

Set up execution logs. Monitor success rate. Track metrics. Alert on failures.

**10. Security**

Webhook secrets. Input validation. Rate limiting. Audit logging.

## Checklist

- [ ] Workflow requirements defined
- [ ] Node structure designed
- [ ] Error handling implemented
- [ ] Credentials configured
- [ ] Testing completed
- [ ] Monitoring set up
- [ ] Documentation created
- [ ] Version control established
- [ ] Rollback plan defined
- [ ] Security reviewed

## Anti Pattern

**1. Monolithic Workflows**

Everything in one workflow. Hard to debug. Hard to maintain. Split into smaller.

**2. No Error Handling**

Ignoring errors. Silent failures. Data loss. Proper error handling.

**3. Hardcoded Values**

Values in workflow. Environment changes break. Use variables. Externalize.

**4. Over-Complex Logic**

Complex expressions. Nested conditions. Hard to read. Simplify or use Code nodes.

## Best Practice

**1. Workflow Structure**

```json
{
  "name": "Order Processing Workflow",
  "nodes": [
    {
      "name": "Webhook Trigger",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.webhook",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [250, 300],
      "webhookId": "order-webhook",
      "parameters": {
        "httpMethod": "POST",
        "path": "orders",
        "responseMode": "onReceived",
        "options": {
          "rawBody": false
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "name": "Validate Order",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.code",
      "position": [500, 300],
      "parameters": {
        "jsCode": "const order = $json;\n\nif (!order.items || order.items.length === 0) {\n  throw new Error('Order must have at least one item');\n}\n\nif (!order.customerId) {\n  throw new Error('Customer ID is required');\n}\n\nreturn { json: { valid: true, order } };"
      }
    },
    {
      "name": "Create Database Record",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.postgres",
      "position": [750, 300],
      "parameters": {
        "operation": "executeQuery",
        "query": "INSERT INTO orders (id, customer_id, status, data) VALUES ($1, $2, $3, $4)",
        "options": {
          "values": {
            "values": [
              { "name": "id", "value": "={{ $json.order.id }}" },
              { "name": "customer_id", "value": "={{ $json.order.customerId }}" },
              { "name": "status", "value": "pending" },
              { "name": "data", "value": "={{ JSON.stringify($json.order) }}" }
            ]
          }
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "name": "Notify Customer",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.email",
      "position": [1000, 200],
      "parameters": {
        "to": "={{ $json.customer.email }}",
        "subject": "Order Confirmation",
        "body": "Your order {{ $json.order.id }} has been received.",
        "options": {}
      }
    },
    {
      "name": "Update Inventory",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.httpRequest",
      "position": [1000, 400],
      "parameters": {
        "method": "POST",
        "url": "={{ $env.INVENTORY_API_URL }}/reserve",
        "bodyParameters": {
          "items": "={{ $json.order.items }}"
        },
        "options": {}
      }
    },
    {
      "name": "Handle Error",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.errorTrigger",
      "position": [1250, 300]
    }
  ],
  "connections": {
    "Webhook Trigger": {
      "main": [[{ "node": "Validate Order", "type": "main", "index": 0 }]]
    },
    "Validate Order": {
      "main": [[{ "node": "Create Database Record", "type": "main", "index": 0 }]]
    },
    "Create Database Record": {
      "main": [
        [{ "node": "Notify Customer", "type": "main", "index": 0 }],
        [{ "node": "Update Inventory", "type": "main", "index": 0 }]
      ]
    }
  },
  "active": true,
  "settings": {
    "executionOrder": "v1"
  }
}
```

**2. Reusable Sub-Workflows**

```json
{
  "name": "Send Email Template",
  "nodes": [
    {
      "name": "Workflow Input",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.workflowTrigger",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [250, 300]
    },
    {
      "name": "Load Template",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.code",
      "position": [500, 300],
      "parameters": {
        "jsCode": "const templates = {\n  welcome: {\n    subject: 'Welcome to {{ company }}!',\n    body: 'Hello {{ name }},\\n\\nWelcome to our platform.'\n  },\n  orderConfirmation: {\n    subject: 'Order {{ orderId }} Confirmed',\n    body: 'Your order is confirmed. Order ID: {{ orderId }}'\n  }\n};\n\nconst template = templates[$input.first().json.template];\nif (!template) {\n  throw new Error(`Template ${$input.first().json.template} not found`);\n}\n\nreturn { json: { ...template, data: $input.first().json } };"
      }
    },
    {
      "name": "Render Template",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.handlebars",
      "position": [750, 300],
      "parameters": {
        "operation": "renderTemplate",
        "template": "={{ $json.subject }}",
        "data": "={{ $json.data }}"
      }
    }
  ]
}
```

**3. Batch Processing Workflow**

```json
{
  "name": "Batch Customer Sync",
  "nodes": [
    {
      "name": "Cron Trigger",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.cron",
      "position": [250, 300],
      "parameters": {
        "rule": {
          "interval": [
            { "triggerAtHour": 2 }
          ]
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "name": "Fetch Customers",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.postgres",
      "position": [500, 300],
      "parameters": {
        "operation": "executeQuery",
        "query": "SELECT id, email, name, updated_at FROM customers WHERE updated_at > NOW() - INTERVAL '24 hours'"
      }
    },
    {
      "name": "Split In Batches",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.splitInBatches",
      "position": [750, 300],
      "parameters": {
        "batchSize": 100
      }
    },
    {
      "name": "Process Batch",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.code",
      "position": [1000, 300],
      "parameters": {
        "jsCode": "// Process batch of customers\nconst customers = $input.all().map(i => i.json);\n\n// Transform for external system\nreturn customers.map(customer => ({\n  json: {\n    external_id: customer.id,\n    email: customer.email,\n    full_name: customer.name,\n    last_updated: customer.updated_at\n  }\n}));"
      }
    },
    {
      "name": "Sync to CRM",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.httpRequest",
      "position": [1250, 300],
      "parameters": {
        "method": "POST",
        "url": "={{ $env.CRM_API_URL }}/contacts/batch",
        "authentication": "genericCredentialType",
        "genericAuthType": "httpHeaderAuth",
        "sendHeaders": true,
        "headerParameters": {
          "parameters": [
            { "name": "Authorization", "value": "Bearer {{ $env.CRM_API_KEY }}" }
          ]
        },
        "bodyParameters": {
          "contacts": "={{ $json }}"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "name": "Log Results",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.googleSheets",
      "position": [1500, 300],
      "parameters": {
        "operation": "append",
        "sheetId": "={{ $env.SHEET_ID }}",
        "range": "A1",
        "options": {
          "valueInputMode": "USER_ENTERED"
        }
      }
    }
  ]
}
```

**4. Error Handling Pattern**

```json
{
  "name": "API Integration with Error Handling",
  "nodes": [
    {
      "name": "Webhook",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.webhook",
      "position": [250, 300]
    },
    {
      "name": "Try Block",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.wait",
      "position": [500, 300],
      "parameters": {
        "amount": 1,
        "unit": "seconds"
      }
    },
    {
      "name": "API Call",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.httpRequest",
      "position": [750, 300],
      "parameters": {
        "method": "POST",
        "url": "={{ $env.API_URL }}/process",
        "options": {
          "timeout": 30000,
          "retry": {
            "maxRetries": 3,
            "retryWaitMax": 10000
          }
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "name": "Success Path",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.noOp",
      "position": [1000, 200],
      "parameters": {}
    },
    {
      "name": "Retry Handler",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.errorTrigger",
      "position": [1000, 400],
      "parameters": {}
    },
    {
      "name": "Send Alert",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.slack",
      "position": [1250, 400],
      "parameters": {
        "channel": "#alerts",
        "text": "=: Execution failed: {{ $json.execution.id }}"
      }
    },
    {
      "name": "Queue for Retry",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.redis",
      "position": [1250, 600],
      "parameters": {
        "operation": "lpush",
        "key": "retry-queue",
        "value": "={{ JSON.stringify($json.execution) }}"
      }
    }
  ]
}
```

